email.task:
You are an IT support technician. More and more staff are using TeamTalk, the company's instant messaging app, on their phones. Mia, a new sales assistant, wants to install it. Write an email to Mia explaining the steps, using the notes below. In your email you must use:
- imperatives and sequence words for the steps;
- at least one sentence describing a current trend (present continuous or more and more);
- at least one second conditional sentence (If + past simple, … would/could + verb), for example to explain what would happen if she didn't set her status to "Away";
- at least one polite request (Could you…? / It would be great if you could…), for example asking Mia to send you a test message.
Follow the standard layout for an email giving instructions: From / To / Date / Subject, a greeting, It should be quite easy to …, the steps with First / Then / Next / After that / Finally, a reminder (Don't forget to … when you've finished.), then Best wishes and your name, position and department.
Write 80–100 words (do not count the From, To, Date and Subject lines).
